## Login prerequisite

Before a protected command, run `{{ .App.Name }} status`:

- Continue when the status is `valid` or `needs_refresh`; the CLI refreshes before the request when needed.
- For `expired` or `not_logged_in`, read and follow [`../cli-auth/SKILL.md`](../cli-auth/SKILL.md), then continue only after `status` reports `valid`.
- If `status` fails, stop the business call and report the error summary.
{{- end }}

## First Steps

1. Run `{{ .App.Name }} {{ .Group.Name }} --help` before choosing a command.
2. Use `{{ .App.Name }} skills list` to discover generated skill names and `{{ .App.Name }} skills read {{ skillName .Group }}` to read the current editable skill file. If not running from the generated project root, pass `--skills-dir <path-to-skills>`.
3. Read [references/commands.md](references/commands.md) for the complete generated command and flag surface.
4. Use [references/command-routing.md](references/command-routing.md) when multiple commands look similar.
5. Use [references/workflows.md](references/workflows.md) for multi-step work; fill its MANUAL sections before relying on business flows.
6. For write, delete, bulk, or irreversible actions, follow the safety rules below and [references/production-checklist.md](references/production-checklist.md).

