- Environment variables are plaintext per-run overrides and take priority over file values
{{- if appUsesAKSK .App }}
- Environment variable `OPENCLI_AK`: AK/SK access key
- Environment variable `OPENCLI_SK`: AK/SK secret key
- Signer profile: `{{ appSignerProfile .App }}`
- AK/SK headers are generated by the CLI: `appKey`, `sign`, `timestamp`, `nonce`
{{- else if appUsesToken .App }}
- Environment variable `OPENCLI_AUTH_TOKEN`: Authentication token
{{- else if appUsesAPIKey .App }}
- Environment variable `OPENCLI_API_KEY`: API-key override; the header name comes from the runtime file
{{- else if appUsesOAuth2 .App }}
{{- if and .RuntimeBundle (eq .RuntimeBundle.OAuth2GrantType "authorization_code") }}
- OAuth 2.0 Authorization Code is used for protected operations
- Run `{{ .App.Name }} status` before invoking protected business commands
- When login is required, read [`../cli-auth/SKILL.md`](../cli-auth/SKILL.md)
- The CLI stores and injects the business access token; IAM credentials are not configured in the CLI
{{- else }}
- OAuth 2.0 Client Credentials is handled automatically for protected operations
- Environment variable `OPENCLI_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET`: plaintext per-run Client Secret override
- The public Client ID and sealed default Client Secret come from `config/runtime.yaml`
{{- end }}
{{- else }}
- No authentication is configured; use `-H` / `--header` only for non-auth internal routing headers when needed
{{- end }}
{{- end }}

